1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,600
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:04,810
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,810 --> 00:00:05,940
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,370 --> 00:00:08,820
I've worked the docks for
thirty-one years.

5
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:11,880
Concrete under my feet and
heavy lifting,

6
00:00:11,880 --> 00:00:13,460
every single shift.

7
00:00:13,590 --> 00:00:14,550
I had my right knee

8
00:00:14,550 --> 00:00:16,050
replaced two years ago.

9
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:18,420
It has hurt every day
since.

10
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:19,860
Not surgery pain.

11
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,340
I know what that felt
like,

12
00:00:21,340 --> 00:00:22,400
and it went away.

13
00:00:22,440 --> 00:00:23,350
This is different.

14
00:00:23,390 --> 00:00:24,060
Tight.

15
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:24,630
Full.

16
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:25,650
Like a band around

17
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:27,540
the joint that never
loosens.

18
00:00:27,630 --> 00:00:28,660
And for two years I've

19
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:30,100
been told the same thing.

20
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:31,050
Give it time.

21
00:00:31,430 --> 00:00:33,740
At six weeks it was
swelling,

22
00:00:33,740 --> 00:00:35,120
and swelling is normal.

23
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,680
At three months,

24
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,720
give it six.

25
00:00:37,760 --> 00:00:38,610
At six months,

26
00:00:38,610 --> 00:00:40,250
some knees take a full
year.

27
00:00:40,290 --> 00:00:41,060
At a year,

28
00:00:41,060 --> 00:00:42,830
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

29
00:00:43,190 --> 00:00:44,560
And I didn't just wait.

30
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:45,900
We went down the list.

31
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:47,520
More physical therapy.

32
00:00:47,720 --> 00:00:48,930
Every session,

33
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:50,390
every exercise at home.

34
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:51,900
I got stronger.

35
00:00:51,940 --> 00:00:53,310
The tightness never moved.

36
00:00:53,350 --> 00:00:54,970
The pain pills helped,

37
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:56,310
and that was the problem.

38
00:00:56,590 --> 00:00:58,500
I'm already on enough
every morning,

39
00:00:58,500 --> 00:00:59,480
and nobody could tell me

40
00:00:59,480 --> 00:01:00,640
when I'd get to stop.

41
00:01:00,980 --> 00:01:02,570
Then a nerve block.

42
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:04,950
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

43
00:01:04,990 --> 00:01:06,450
And after that, a second

44
00:01:06,450 --> 00:01:07,570
operation to go back

45
00:01:07,570 --> 00:01:08,510
in and do it over.

46
00:01:08,550 --> 00:01:09,480
I said no.

47
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:10,880
Every morning I climbed
out

48
00:01:10,880 --> 00:01:12,180
of my truck at the port

49
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:13,120
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:14,850
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:17,110
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:17,310 --> 00:01:18,480
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,480 --> 00:01:19,800
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:22,390
Couldn't climb the gangway
without stopping,

55
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:23,660
couldn't stand a full
shift

56
00:01:23,660 --> 00:01:25,820
on the dock without
leaning on something,

57
00:01:25,820 --> 00:01:27,840
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:27,840 --> 00:01:29,700
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,030
The younger guys on my
crew started

60
00:01:32,030 --> 00:01:33,830
taking the heavy lifts for
me.

61
00:01:33,980 --> 00:01:35,430
It woke me at night,

62
00:01:35,430 --> 00:01:37,670
and it turned ordinary
things,

63
00:01:37,670 --> 00:01:38,960
like getting in the truck

64
00:01:38,960 --> 00:01:40,330
or up off the couch,

65
00:01:40,330 --> 00:01:41,490
into a decision.

66
00:01:41,800 --> 00:01:43,330
After a long and serious

67
00:01:43,330 --> 00:01:44,870
talk with my wife,

68
00:01:44,870 --> 00:01:47,260
I went back in one more
time.

69
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:48,880
That was the fourth set

70
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:50,570
of X-rays on this knee.

71
00:01:50,730 --> 00:01:52,140
And like the three before
it,

72
00:01:52,140 --> 00:01:54,820
the answer was everything
looks great.

73
00:01:54,860 --> 00:01:56,770
No loosening, no
infection,

74
00:01:56,770 --> 00:01:57,690
nothing wrong.

75
00:01:57,970 --> 00:01:59,110
Only this time there

76
00:01:59,110 --> 00:02:00,250
was no new number.

77
00:02:00,540 --> 00:02:02,550
Nobody said give it
another six months.

78
00:02:02,590 --> 00:02:04,580
There was nothing left to
give it.

79
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:05,570
I sat in the parking

80
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,430
lot for a while.

81
00:02:06,470 --> 00:02:07,440
Okay, I thought.

82
00:02:07,610 --> 00:02:08,750
Then explain this.

83
00:02:08,790 --> 00:02:10,140
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

84
00:02:10,140 --> 00:02:11,460
I hit my breaking point.

85
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,700
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

86
00:02:13,880 --> 00:02:15,100
I had an early shift

87
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:16,080
on the docks.

88
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:18,150
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:18,150 --> 00:02:20,310
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:20,310 --> 00:02:21,560
with my leg up,

91
00:02:21,560 --> 00:02:23,410
trying to find any angle

92
00:02:23,410 --> 00:02:24,790
where it didn't feel like
something

93
00:02:24,790 --> 00:02:26,740
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

94
00:02:26,780 --> 00:02:29,030
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

95
00:02:29,180 --> 00:02:30,820
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

96
00:02:31,270 --> 00:02:32,520
And I just thought,

97
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,250
is this really my life
now?

98
00:02:34,290 --> 00:02:35,760
I can't live like this.

99
00:02:35,890 --> 00:02:37,980
So I made myself a
promise.

100
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,100
I wouldn't go a day

101
00:02:39,100 --> 00:02:40,710
without looking for an
answer.

102
00:02:40,900 --> 00:02:42,400
And when I found one,

103
00:02:42,400 --> 00:02:43,550
I'd share it with everyone

104
00:02:43,550 --> 00:02:44,820
going through the same
thing.

105
00:02:44,860 --> 00:02:46,570
So I got my laptop

106
00:02:46,570 --> 00:02:47,900
out and went looking.

107
00:02:48,170 --> 00:02:49,440
Not for a product.

108
00:02:49,510 --> 00:02:50,700
For an explanation.

109
00:02:50,950 --> 00:02:52,500
Mayo Clinic forums,

110
00:02:52,500 --> 00:02:54,850
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

111
00:02:54,850 --> 00:02:57,640
doctor videos, medical
animations.

112
00:02:58,030 --> 00:02:59,100
And that's when I found

113
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,140
a video from a physical
therapist

114
00:03:01,140 --> 00:03:01,680
named Dr.

115
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:03,190
Steven Salinger,

116
00:03:03,190 --> 00:03:04,480
whose own wife

117
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:06,440
had been through exactly
this.

118
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:08,530
But before I say anything
else,

119
00:03:08,530 --> 00:03:09,910
I want to be straight with
you.

120
00:03:10,020 --> 00:03:12,170
You've already had
something work fast.

121
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:13,160
The ice.

122
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,850
The first week of a new
pill.

123
00:03:14,890 --> 00:03:16,270
The good day after a
session.

124
00:03:16,310 --> 00:03:17,540
Then it wore off.

125
00:03:17,740 --> 00:03:20,010
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

126
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:22,070
Fast relief isn't relief.

127
00:03:22,220 --> 00:03:23,170
It's a preview.

128
00:03:23,450 --> 00:03:24,730
So I'm not going to tell

129
00:03:24,730 --> 00:03:25,910
you this works fast.

130
00:03:25,950 --> 00:03:26,810
It doesn't.

131
00:03:26,980 --> 00:03:28,760
But if you're willing to
be patient,

132
00:03:28,760 --> 00:03:29,910
and to look at what's
going

133
00:03:29,910 --> 00:03:31,460
on around your new knee

134
00:03:31,460 --> 00:03:33,120
instead of inside it,
there

135
00:03:33,120 --> 00:03:35,340
is a real reason it still
hurts.

136
00:03:35,460 --> 00:03:37,080
And something you can do
about it.

137
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:38,860
Let me explain what he
said,

138
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,150
because this is what
changed

139
00:03:40,150 --> 00:03:41,290
everything for me.

140
00:03:41,570 --> 00:03:43,230
He started with the
basics.

141
00:03:43,340 --> 00:03:44,720
A knee replacement takes
out

142
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:46,380
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

143
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:47,740
in metal and plastic.

144
00:03:47,920 --> 00:03:49,700
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

145
00:03:49,700 --> 00:03:51,320
you had before the
operation.

146
00:03:51,550 --> 00:03:52,960
That part I already knew.

147
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:54,340
But then he explained
something

148
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:55,900
nobody had ever told me.

149
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:56,400
He said,

150
00:03:56,400 --> 00:03:57,810
think about a swollen foot

151
00:03:57,810 --> 00:03:58,820
inside a shoe.

152
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:00,160
The shoe didn't shrink.

153
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:02,150
Your foot is taking up
more room,

154
00:04:02,150 --> 00:04:03,600
so everything feels
cramped

155
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:05,140
and tight and squeezed.

156
00:04:05,190 --> 00:04:06,140
Your new knee sits

157
00:04:06,140 --> 00:04:07,540
in a limited space

158
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,830
with living tissue packed
all around it.

159
00:04:09,870 --> 00:04:11,330
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

160
00:04:11,330 --> 00:04:12,930
had to work through that
tissue.

161
00:04:13,220 --> 00:04:15,530
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

162
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:17,040
At first that's normal.

163
00:04:17,210 --> 00:04:19,040
But in some people that
swelling can

164
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:21,670
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

165
00:04:22,140 --> 00:04:23,930
And swollen tissue takes
up more

166
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:25,820
room than calm tissue
does.

167
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:27,470
So when you bend,

168
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:29,240
that tissue gets
compressed.

169
00:04:29,370 --> 00:04:30,430
When you straighten,

170
00:04:30,430 --> 00:04:31,620
it gets pulled tight.

171
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:32,610
That's the band.

172
00:04:32,650 --> 00:04:34,660
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

173
00:04:34,700 --> 00:04:35,420
And you start being

174
00:04:35,420 --> 00:04:36,370
the one who says,

175
00:04:36,370 --> 00:04:37,290
you go ahead.

176
00:04:37,390 --> 00:04:38,330
I'll stay here.

177
00:04:38,470 --> 00:04:40,020
And that's exactly why so
much

178
00:04:40,020 --> 00:04:42,300
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

179
00:04:42,720 --> 00:04:44,690
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

180
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:45,710
around the knee.

181
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:46,800
Worth doing,

182
00:04:46,800 --> 00:04:47,930
and I'd done it.

183
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,540
It does nothing about
tissue

184
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:50,640
taking up room.

185
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,940
A nerve block quiets

186
00:04:51,940 --> 00:04:53,830
the nerve carrying the
signal.

187
00:04:54,070 --> 00:04:55,780
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

188
00:04:56,250 --> 00:04:57,950
But when that irritated
tissue

189
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,470
finally calms down,

190
00:04:59,470 --> 00:05:00,960
it holds less fluid,

191
00:05:00,960 --> 00:05:02,460
and it takes up less room.

192
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:05,640
Less room taken up means
less pressure

193
00:05:05,640 --> 00:05:06,960
squeezing the joint.

194
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:08,720
That's what takes the
pressure off.

195
00:05:09,170 --> 00:05:10,710
After two years of this,

196
00:05:10,710 --> 00:05:12,390
it finally made sense.

197
00:05:12,660 --> 00:05:14,630
The problem was never the
new knee.

198
00:05:14,710 --> 00:05:16,640
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

199
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:18,240
He calls it the squeeze.

200
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,850
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

201
00:05:21,090 --> 00:05:22,380
I'd bought knee sleeves,

202
00:05:22,380 --> 00:05:23,530
work boot insoles,

203
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:25,670
compression braces,
creams,

204
00:05:25,670 --> 00:05:27,380
half of Amazon really,

205
00:05:27,380 --> 00:05:28,580
and all any of it gave

206
00:05:28,580 --> 00:05:29,610
me was an hour.

207
00:05:29,770 --> 00:05:30,720
I even looked at going

208
00:05:30,720 --> 00:05:32,620
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

209
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,250
But at $200 a session

210
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:36,170
with nothing covered by
insurance,

211
00:05:36,170 --> 00:05:37,330
that was a quick no.

212
00:05:37,790 --> 00:05:38,820
Then one night I went

213
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,030
back to that knee
replacement

214
00:05:40,030 --> 00:05:41,360
group and actually read
it.

215
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:43,010
Thousands of people,

216
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:44,760
years out from surgery,

217
00:05:44,760 --> 00:05:47,260
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

218
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:48,660
nobody could explain.

219
00:05:48,700 --> 00:05:50,650
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

220
00:05:50,650 --> 00:05:52,290
the same thing kept coming
up.

221
00:05:52,620 --> 00:05:54,830
This one device,

222
00:05:54,830 --> 00:05:56,300
and people saying it was
the first

223
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:57,610
thing that made a
difference.

224
00:05:57,670 --> 00:05:59,430
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

225
00:05:59,430 --> 00:06:00,370
alright, here it comes,

226
00:06:00,370 --> 00:06:01,620
he's selling me something,

227
00:06:01,620 --> 00:06:03,170
let me shut that down
right now.

228
00:06:03,450 --> 00:06:05,170
I'm only here because I
made myself

229
00:06:05,170 --> 00:06:07,100
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

230
00:06:07,100 --> 00:06:07,970
that if I ever found

231
00:06:07,970 --> 00:06:09,140
something that helped,

232
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:10,070
I'd say so.

233
00:06:10,520 --> 00:06:11,920
It's called the KenRelief
Red

234
00:06:11,920 --> 00:06:13,140
Light Therapy Wrap.

235
00:06:13,180 --> 00:06:14,980
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

236
00:06:15,280 --> 00:06:17,010
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

237
00:06:17,010 --> 00:06:19,110
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

238
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,440
But I went to their
website anyway,

239
00:06:21,440 --> 00:06:22,360
just to see what all

240
00:06:22,360 --> 00:06:23,440
the fuss was about.

241
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,900
It's the same

242
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:26,830
red light therapy clinics

243
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:29,330
charge $200 a session

244
00:06:29,330 --> 00:06:30,850
for, off machines that
cost

245
00:06:30,850 --> 00:06:32,540
fifty thousand dollars,

246
00:06:32,540 --> 00:06:33,540
in a wrap you plug

247
00:06:33,540 --> 00:06:34,790
into the wall at home.

248
00:06:35,030 --> 00:06:36,710
Two hundred and forty
lights.

249
00:06:36,860 --> 00:06:38,630
Red at 660 nanometers

250
00:06:38,630 --> 00:06:40,750
and near-infrared at 850,

251
00:06:40,750 --> 00:06:42,720
run together for the
strongest effect.

252
00:06:42,830 --> 00:06:44,240
Four strength levels.

253
00:06:44,330 --> 00:06:45,930
A five to thirty minute
timer.

254
00:06:45,970 --> 00:06:48,030
Then I saw the guarantee.

255
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,570
Ninety days.

256
00:06:49,610 --> 00:06:51,970
Results or your money
back,

257
00:06:51,970 --> 00:06:53,280
no questions,

258
00:06:53,280 --> 00:06:54,670
no store credit,

259
00:06:54,670 --> 00:06:56,490
and you don't even send it
back.

260
00:06:56,810 --> 00:06:59,060
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

261
00:06:59,060 --> 00:07:00,670
days to change my mind.

262
00:07:00,810 --> 00:07:02,380
There wasn't much to lose,

263
00:07:02,380 --> 00:07:03,540
so I ordered it.

264
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,890
Two of them, actually.

265
00:07:05,180 --> 00:07:07,160
Only the right knee was
replaced,

266
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:09,730
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

267
00:07:09,730 --> 00:07:10,680
and I'd done it on every

268
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,010
shift for two years.

269
00:07:12,230 --> 00:07:14,270
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:14,510 --> 00:07:15,430
When it came,

271
00:07:15,430 --> 00:07:17,590
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:17,590 --> 00:07:18,750
because I'd been let down

273
00:07:18,750 --> 00:07:20,570
too many times to get
excited.

274
00:07:20,770 --> 00:07:22,340
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:22,530 --> 00:07:24,460
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:24,700 --> 00:07:26,180
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:26,180 --> 00:07:27,670
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:27,940 --> 00:07:28,970
And that was it.

279
00:07:29,120 --> 00:07:30,860
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:30,950 --> 00:07:32,300
When I took it off,

281
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:32,980
I'll be honest,

282
00:07:32,980 --> 00:07:34,650
nothing dramatic had
happened.

283
00:07:34,710 --> 00:07:36,360
And after what that video
said,

284
00:07:36,360 --> 00:07:38,460
that's exactly what I
expected.

285
00:07:38,670 --> 00:07:40,180
What was different

286
00:07:40,180 --> 00:07:41,110
was that for the first

287
00:07:41,110 --> 00:07:42,480
time in two years

288
00:07:42,480 --> 00:07:44,240
I'd done something for my
knee

289
00:07:44,240 --> 00:07:45,370
